  "Question": "What characterizes 2 quantities that are directly proportional?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "Their ratio is constant",
    "B": "Their product is constant",
    "C": "Their sum is constant"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "When speed is constant, distance and time are directly proportional. For positive travel time,\n\\[\n\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{time}}=\\text{speed}\n\\]\nis constant. A constant ratio is the defining property of directly proportional quantities, wherever the ratio is defined. Therefore the answer is A.",
